From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Add the Epson S1C33

Calls, ffi_call, for every type, variadic calls included, as the C33 port
of GCC makes them: arguments in %r6-%r9 (an 8-byte one may run on into
%r10, except a double, which then goes on the stack), the rest and
aggregates without a scalar mode on the stack in order, a variadic call
with every unnamed argument (and the last named one) on the stack and in
no register, results in %r4:%r5 or to memory through a hidden first
argument.  Under FDPIC the call takes the function descriptor's data
pointer, as GCC's own indirect calls do.  No closures yet.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: N/A the C33 has no upstream GCC port

--- a/Makefile.am
+++ b/Makefile.am
@@ -70,12 +70,14 @@
 	src/wasm/ffitarget.h \
 	src/x86/ffitarget.h src/x86/internal.h src/x86/internal64.h	\
 	src/x86/asmnames.h src/xtensa/ffitarget.h src/dlmalloc.c	\
+	src/c33/ffitarget.h						\
 	src/kvx/ffitarget.h src/kvx/asm.h				\
 	src/loongarch/ffitarget.h
 
 EXTRA_libffi_la_SOURCES = src/aarch64/ffi.c src/aarch64/sysv.S		\
 	src/aarch64/win64_armasm.S src/alpha/ffi.c src/alpha/osf.S	\
 	src/arc/ffi.c src/arc/arcompact.S src/arm/ffi.c			\
+	src/c33/ffi.c src/c33/sysv.S					\
 	src/arm/sysv.S src/arm/ffi.c src/arm/sysv_msvc_arm32.S		\
 	src/avr32/ffi.c src/avr32/sysv.S src/bfin/ffi.c			\
 	src/bfin/sysv.S src/cris/ffi.c src/cris/sysv.S src/frv/ffi.c	\
--- a/configure.host
